2.42.0

```

When `wlr_surface_set_preferred_buffer_scale` or `wlr_surface_set_preferred_buffer_transform` is invoked from these two places, wezterm crashes. Sadly I dont know more about wayland to proceed. 

It seems the cause was proper support for wl_compositor v6, is there something that needs to be done by wezterm to support that?

@participant9 see here for more on this: https://github.com/participant8/wezterm/issues/4504

Basically, upgrading smithay client toolkit to 0.16.1 is what fixed the issue. Unfortunately, there are other issues with that version. There's no obvious other way to fix those without upgrading sctk to 0.17 or 0.18 (and that's a big undertaking as the api:s changed significantly - so, need a full rewrite of the wayland support in wezterm).

Unfortunately it means wayland support in wezterm is quite bad at the moment.

Until them, is it not possible to [do like the BSD solution](
https://<redacted-host>/ports/diff/x11/wezterm/files/patch-sctk?id=5c9692ca786cc9e0c9c9ff9c67cab97cb68b422b) and simply ignore the  wl_surface::Event::preferred_buffer_scale?
   
